  "text": "11. The Constitution (One Hundred and First) Amendment Act, 2016 was required to be\nratified by the Legislature of not less than one half of the State Legislatures because it\nsought to make changes in:\n(i) Chapter | of Part XI of the Constitution dealing with legislative relations\nbetween the Union and the States.\n(ii) Lists | and Il of the Seventh Schedule to the Constitution.\n(iii) the Sixth Schedule to the Constitution.\n(iv) Part XIIl of the Constitution dealing with trade, commerce and intercourse\nwithin India.\nSelect the correct answer from the following:\nA. All the four reasons\nB. It was not required to be ratified by the State Legislatures before being\npresented to the President for assent.\nC. (ii) only\nD. (i) and (ii) only",
